Sonia: Three years and a failed cycle is a long time to keep going with, and you've been carrying most of it yourself by the sound of it.

Was anything changed after the IVF, or was it the same plan repeated?

Lead: same plan, they just said try again.

Sonia: Then there's a whole half of it that nobody has been through with you, and that is the part worth going into properly.

DO NOT WRITE THIS

Sonia: The first step is a free consultation with my team, who take your full history and decide whether I can help. Shall I send you the link?

Nothing in the conversation has told her this is paid. Naming the call, the first step, or the team as the way in is the invitation, whether or not a link is attached, and she is being asked to spend an hour before she knows there is a fee at the end of it. That it is paid comes first, in a message of its own, every time.

ALSO DO NOT WRITE THIS

The same message with the price range dropped into it, on a turn where she has asked how the program works and nothing else.

She asked what it is, and a figure is the answer to a different question. Volunteering it turns an explanation into a quote and makes her respond to a number before she has decided she wants the thing. Tell her it is paid and that the support level varies. She will ask what it costs when she wants to know, and then you give the range without hedging it.
